  <name>Nib</name>
  <summary>Use your tablet as a stylus-ready second display for GNOME</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      Nib turns your Android tablet or phone into a low-latency external display
      for GNOME, with full touch, gesture, and active stylus/pencil support.
    </p>
    <p>Features:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Hardware-accelerated, low-latency video streaming</li>
      <li>Extend your GNOME desktop or mirror your main display</li>
      <li>Multi-finger trackpad gestures: click, right-click, scroll, and workspace switching</li>
      <li>Pressure- and tilt-aware stylus input for Krita, GIMP, and Inkscape</li>
      <li>Connect over USB or Wi-Fi, with support for multiple devices at once</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
