  <releases>
    <release version="0.1.3" date="2026-09-09">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Several tablets can now stream at once without competing for the same ports</li>
          <li>Stopping screen sharing from GNOME's own system menu is now noticed, instead of leaving Nib stuck on "streaming"</li>
          <li>Connection problems are now reported, rather than leaving a stream that silently carries nothing</li>
          <li>The tablet app notices when the connection drops and reconnects on its own</li>
          <li>The streamed image no longer freezes on an otherwise idle desktop</li>
          <li>Lower latency on touch, stylus and gesture input</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.1.2" date="2026-07-28">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Fixed a black picture on the tablet when running as a Flatpak</li>
          <li>Software video encoding is now used under sandboxing, where the drivers the hardware encoders need are unavailable</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.1.1" date="2026-07-28">
